notes:
These are primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

GMO's third, fourth and fourteenth reports cover the unauthorized access, the extortion and compensation, and the bounty and device analysis. @IT's report of the November 2 press conference, in Japanese, gives GMO's timeline. Kyodo News, carried by The Straits Times, reports the attribution, and GovInfoSecurity the bounty and the attacker's claims. Finance Magnates covers the brokers' responses, and Microsoft documents drive redirection.

The page also cites GMO's other reports and its loss compensation notice, Kumagai's blog, Dempa Shimbun, IBTimes citing NHK, Microsoft's list of supported RDP properties, and the MITRE pages for T1072 and T1039.

The background slides name their own sources, all from MITRE ATT&CK.

